WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:16.617
"I have a confession to make," Luke went on.

2
00:00:16.618 --> 00:00:21.572
"I knew it!" Maggie exclaimed. "You took those tickets, didn't you?"

3
00:00:21.573 --> 00:00:24.550
"What?" Luke looked confused.

4
00:00:24.551 --> 00:00:30.132
"No, wait. My confession is that I already saw Revenge of the Pirate's Ghost.

5
00:00:30.133 --> 00:00:33.086
My uncle owns a movie theater in my hometown.

6
00:00:33.087 --> 00:00:36.331
He held an early screening, and I got to go."

7
00:00:36.332 --> 00:00:40.914
Henry was surprised. That wasn't the confession he'd expected!

8
00:00:40.915 --> 00:00:47.147
"Wait," Henry said. "You already saw the movie? Why didn't you tell us?"

9
00:00:47.148 --> 00:00:52.219
Luke shrugged. "I didn't want to give away any secrets about the plot.

10
00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:58.366
Especially anything important, like Captain Green is actually the main pirate's brother . . . Oops!"

11
00:00:58.367 --> 00:01:00.855
He clapped one hand over his mouth.

12
00:01:00.856 --> 00:01:03.843
Then he pulled it away, looking sheepish.

13
00:01:03.844 --> 00:01:06.315
"Don't tell Nathan I just said that, okay?

14
00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:09.041
He's really excited to see the movie.

15
00:01:09.042 --> 00:01:11.670
I don't want to ruin the surprise for him.

16
00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:14.659
Sorry I just ruined it for you guys."

17
00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:21.366
"It's okay, and don't worry, we won't tell Nathan," Cole promised while Henry and Maggie nodded.

18
00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:24.137
"But does this mean you didn't take our booty?"

19
00:01:24.138 --> 00:01:30.843
"Of course not!" Luke said. "Why would I do that? I'm not a thief."

20
00:01:30.844 --> 00:01:35.911
He hurried to rejoin the others. Henry looked at Maggie and Cole.

21
00:01:35.912 --> 00:01:38.788
"I guess Luke's innocent," he said.

22
00:01:38.789 --> 00:01:43.817
"If he already saw that movie, he has no motive for stealing the tickets."

23
00:01:43.818 --> 00:01:49.254
"Yeah," Maggie agreed. "Especially since his uncle owns a movie theater.

24
00:01:49.255 --> 00:01:56.080
He can see any movie whenever he wants."

25
00:01:56.081 --> 00:02:00.671
A few minutes later the whole group reached the town of Sea Cove.

26
00:02:00.672 --> 00:02:04.643
Maggie hurried over to Anna and Luke, who were looking at the drawing.

27
00:02:04.644 --> 00:02:08.874
Cole was about to go over there too. But Henry grabbed his arm.

28
00:02:08.875 --> 00:02:12.654
"Look," he said, pointing to a shop nearby.

29
00:02:12.655 --> 00:02:17.450
"Sea Cove General Store," Cole said, reading the sign on the front.

30
00:02:17.451 --> 00:02:20.243
"That must be Anna's family's store."

31
00:02:20.244 --> 00:02:26.987
"That's not all," Henry said. "Look at the initials—SCGS.

32
00:02:26.988 --> 00:02:32.359
That's where Roger got that soda cup. Let's go find out!"

33
00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:38.138
They hurried toward the store. When they got closer, Henry could see it wasn't just a store.

34
00:02:38.139 --> 00:02:42.793
There was a sandwich shop, a catering business, and a soda fountain.

35
00:02:42.794 --> 00:02:47.535
"Wow, Anna's family sure must be busy," he commented.

36
00:02:47.536 --> 00:02:53.336
Cole didn't answer. He was looking in another direction. "Here comes William."

37
00:02:53.337 --> 00:02:56.527
Henry looked and saw William walking toward them.

38
00:02:56.528 --> 00:03:01.290
"Let's try to question him while he's alone," he whispered to Cole.

39
00:03:01.291 --> 00:03:04.324
When William got closer, Henry smiled.

40
00:03:04.325 --> 00:03:09.530
"Hi, William. Are your new shoes more comfortable?" he said.

41
00:03:09.531 --> 00:03:11.987
They all looked down at William's feet.

42
00:03:11.988 --> 00:03:15.479
He was wearing the same shoes he'd had on all day.

43
00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:22.482
"I couldn't find my other sandals," William mumbled. "So I just left these on."

44
00:03:22.483 --> 00:03:25.840
"Are you sure that's what happened?" Cole said.

45
00:03:25.841 --> 00:03:30.365
"Or were you really hiding something in your room?"

46
00:03:30.366 --> 00:03:34.916
"Hiding something? What do you mean?" William asked.

47
00:03:34.917 --> 00:03:39.906
Henry elbowed Cole. Henry didn't want Cole to give away their suspicions.

48
00:03:39.907 --> 00:03:44.450
But Cole ignored him. "Did you take those movie tickets, William?"

49
00:03:44.451 --> 00:03:50.535
"What?" William looked confused. "Of course not! Why would I do that?"

50
00:03:50.536 --> 00:03:53.462
"We don't know," Henry spoke up.

51
00:03:53.463 --> 00:03:57.478
"But we've noticed that you don't seem very happy to have us here.

52
00:03:57.479 --> 00:04:01.068
Maybe you changed your mind about inviting us."

53
00:04:01.069 --> 00:04:03.270
"Yeah," Cole added.

54
00:04:03.271 --> 00:04:06.885
"Maybe you're trying to ruin the treasure hunt so we'll leave early."

55
00:04:06.886 --> 00:04:14.030
William looked upset. "No way!" he blurted out. "I'm glad you guys are here!"

56
00:04:14.031 --> 00:04:18.863
"Then why have you been in such a bad mood all day?" Cole asked.

57
00:04:18.864 --> 00:04:24.847
William sighed. "Sorry about that. It's because of my parents.

58
00:04:24.848 --> 00:04:29.181
They're used to spending lots of money entertaining people for Dad's job.

59
00:04:29.182 --> 00:04:32.036
I didn't want them to do that this weekend.

60
00:04:32.037 --> 00:04:36.784
I just wanted us to have a fun, normal weekend at the beach." He shrugged.

61
00:04:36.785 --> 00:04:40.873
"But they planned this whole expensive treasure hunt without even telling me!

62
00:04:40.874 --> 00:04:44.319
I was afraid you'd all think I was showing off."

63
00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:47.879
"Is that why you kept disappearing?" Cole asked.

64
00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:52.589
William nodded. "I was trying to get them to tell me what else they have planned.

65
00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:55.082
But they wouldn't tell me anything."

66
00:04:55.083 --> 00:04:58.008
Henry could tell William was being truthful.

67
00:04:58.009 --> 00:05:01.797
"Don't worry. We didn't think you were showing off."

68
00:05:01.798 --> 00:05:08.752
"Yeah. The treasure hunt is fantastic." Cole clapped William on the shoulder.

69
00:05:08.753 --> 00:05:11.697
"Anyway, we like you no matter what."

70
00:05:11.698 --> 00:05:16.999
Henry nodded. "We don't care how much money your parents spend," he added.

71
00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.864
"We came because you're our friend."

72
00:05:19.865 --> 00:05:23.346
William looked relieved. "Thanks.

73
00:05:23.347 --> 00:05:28.044
In that case I'll be in a better mood from now on," he promised.

74
00:05:28.045 --> 00:05:32.728
"Good." Henry smiled. Then he realized something.

75
00:05:32.729 --> 00:05:36.625
"This means we still don't know who took those tickets."

76
00:05:36.626 --> 00:05:40.638
"Is Roger Redbeard still a suspect?" William asked.

77
00:05:40.639 --> 00:05:49.249
"Because when I was leaving my house just now, I saw him lurking around outside!"
